export const title = "HTTP";
export const html = "<h1>HTTP</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>When an event occurs, the device can upload event information and files such as snapshot images to an HTTP server located outside the device.</p>\n<p>The message to upload can be easily edited using token variables.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>HTTP</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Setting the action type to <strong>HTTP</strong> reveals the related settings below it.</p>\n\n<h2>1. URL Settings</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:640px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:130px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Method</span><select disabled><option>GET</option><option>POST</option><option>PUT</option></select>\n    <span>URL</span><span><select disabled style=\"width:80px;\"><option>HTTPS</option></select> <input value=\"https://indoai.ai/api\" disabled></span>\n    <span>2nd URL</span><span><select disabled style=\"width:80px;\"><option>HTTPS</option></select> <input placeholder=\"Request here on failure (optional)\" disabled></span>\n    <span>Validate Server Certificate</span><select disabled><option>On</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>Set the URL and method for the HTTP API request</figcaption>\n</div>\n<p>Set the URL information and method for the HTTP API.</p>\n<p>When the protocol is set to <strong>HTTPS</strong>, the certificate validation field becomes active.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2nd URL</h3>\n<p>If a 2nd URL is configured, the request is automatically retried against the 2nd URL only if the request to the primary URL fails.</p>\n<p>If the request to the primary URL succeeds, no request is made to the 2nd URL.</p>\n<p>The 2nd URL is not a required field &ndash; you don't need to configure it.</p>\n\n<h2>2. Authentication</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:420px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:110px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Authentication</span><select disabled><option>None</option><option>Basic</option><option>Digest</option></select>\n    <span>Username</span><input disabled>\n    <span>Password</span><input disabled>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>Supported authentication methods are None, Basic, and Digest.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Delayed Message Sending</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:260px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:100px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Action Delay</span><span>0</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>After the event occurs, the message is sent after being delayed by the time set in <strong>Action Delay</strong>.</p>\n<p>In most cases you can leave this at its default value of 0.</p>\n\n<h2>4. Displaying Event Data</h2>\n<p>You can embed event information in the API request data.</p>\n<p>Enter event data values using predefined tokens.</p>\n<p>Select the token for the value you want from the combo box, then click the Add button.</p>\n<p>The selected token value is added in the form <code>{{token}}</code>.</p>\n<p>When the actual data is sent, this part is replaced with the corresponding event data.</p>\n<p>Tokens can only be used in fields that support entry through the combo box.</p>\n\n<h2>5. Custom Header Settings</h2>\n<p>To configure headers, click the <strong>Set</strong> button next to Custom Header.</p>\n<p>You can use event data tokens on the header settings page.</p>\n<p>To use a token, select the text field, then add the token. Tokens can only be used in the Value field.</p>\n\n<h2>6. Query Settings</h2>\n<p>The Query String can also be configured the same way as headers.</p>\n<p>Once configured, you can see a brief summary of the query string.</p>\n\n<h2>7. Content-Type</h2>\n<p>Selecting a Content-Type changes the settings page to match that type.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Content-Type: multipart/form-data</h3>\n<p><strong>Form Field Settings</strong> &ndash; to configure the data, click the <strong>Set</strong> button. Clicking Set opens the settings window, where you can use event data tokens to set values. Ready-to-use templates are also provided.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-weight:700;\">&#8251; Snapshot Settings</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">multipart/form-data provides a snapshot attachment feature.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">Content-Type: application/json</h3>\n<p>application/json provides both the event data token feature and a template feature. A JSON-format template is also provided.</p>\n\n<h2>8. Testing the Message</h2>\n<p>Click the Test button at the bottom to test the configured settings. Success or failure is shown briefly at the top of the screen.</p>";
